 Components to Build

 1. FlashManager Backend (Spring Boot + Kotlin)

 Location: STAR/FlashManager/backend/

 Tech Stack (mirrors Projectum):
 - Kotlin 1.8.22 + JVM 17
 - Spring Boot 3.1.5
 - Spring GraphQL (primary API)
 - PostgreSQL 15 + JPA/Hibernate
 - Spring Security + JWT (jjwt)
 - Flyway migrations
 - Gradle Kotlin DSL

 Entities (JPA):
 - User - Web UI users
 - Device - Registered local devices (agents)
 - BuildJob - ESP32/Pi5/Android/backend builds
 - FlashJob - Flash operations queue
 - BuildLog - Build output logs
 - FlashHistory - Completed flash operations

 GraphQL Schema (key operations):
 # Queries
 devices: [Device!]!
 buildJobs(status: JobStatus): [BuildJob!]!
 flashJobs(status: JobStatus): [FlashJob!]!
 buildLogs(buildJobId: ID!): [BuildLog!]!

 # Mutations (Web UI)
 triggerBuild(component: Component!, branch: String): BuildJob!
 createFlashJob(buildJobId: ID!, deviceId: ID!): FlashJob!
 registerDevice(name: String!): DeviceRegistration!

 # Mutations (Agent)
 deviceLogin(apiKey: String!): AuthPayload!
 pollFlashJobs: [FlashJob!]!
 updateFlashStatus(jobId: ID!, status: JobStatus!, message: String): FlashJob!

 # Subscriptions (Real-time)
 buildLogStream(buildJobId: ID!): BuildLog!
 flashJobUpdated(deviceId: ID!): FlashJob!
 deviceStatusChanged: Device!

 Services:
 - BuildService - Triggers builds (ESP32, Pi5, Android, backends)
 - FlashJobService - Manages flash job queue
 - DeviceService - Device registration and status
 - BinaryStorageService - Stores compiled binaries
 - BuildLogService - Streams build output

 Controllers:
 - GraphQL resolvers (primary)
 - REST endpoint for binary downloads (streaming large files)

 2. FlashManager Frontend (React + TypeScript)

 Location: STAR/FlashManager/frontend/

 Tech Stack (mirrors Projectum):
 - React 19.1.1 + TypeScript
 - Vite 7.1.7
 - Apollo Client 4.0.7 (GraphQL + subscriptions)
 - Redux Toolkit 2.9.0 (auth state)
 - Tailwind CSS 3.4.17
 - Recharts (build statistics)

 Pages:
 - /login - User authentication
 - /dashboard - Overview (active builds, devices, flash queue)
 - /builds - Build management and history
 - /builds/:id/logs - Real-time build log viewer
 - /flash - Flash job queue and history
 - /devices - Device management and registration

 Key Components:
 - BuildTrigger - Select component and trigger build
 - BuildLogViewer - Real-time streaming logs (GraphQL subscription)
 - FlashJobQueue - Drag-and-drop flash job creation
 - DeviceStatus - Live device connection status
 - FlashHistory - Historical flash operations

 GraphQL Integration:
 - Apollo Client setup (same as Projectum)
 - GraphQL-WS for subscriptions
 - Optimistic updates for better UX

 3. Local Flash Agent (Rust)

 Location: STAR/FlashAgent/

 Features:
 - Cross-platform binary (Mac, Windows, Linux)
 - GraphQL client (reqwest + graphql_client)
 - JWT authentication
 - Device registration on first run
 - Poll-based flash job checking (every 5s)
 - Binary download and caching
 - Hardware detection (serialport-rs)
 - Flash implementations:
   - ESP32: esptool.py wrapper
   - Pi5 SD: dd wrapper (requires sudo)
   - Android: adb install wrapper
 - Status reporting to backend
 - Local config file (~/.star-flash-agent.toml)

 CLI Interface:
 flash-agent register              # Register device with backend
 flash-agent start                 # Start polling daemon
 flash-agent status                # Show connection status
 flash-agent devices               # List local USB devices
 flash-agent config                # View/edit configuration

 4. Coder Template

 Location: STAR/.coder/coder.yaml

 Base Image: Custom Dockerfile with:
 - Ubuntu 22.04
 - ESP-IDF v5.5.1
 - Buildroot 2025.02
 - Android SDK + Gradle
 - JDK 17 + Gradle
 - Node.js 20 + npm
 - Rust toolchain
 - PostgreSQL client tools

 Startup Scripts:
 - Start PostgreSQL container
 - Start FlashManager backend (port 8081)
 - Start FlashManager frontend (port 5174)
 - Display access URLs and setup instructions

 5. Database Schema

 Migrations: backend/src/main/resources/db/migration/

 V1__initial_schema.sql:
   - users (id, email, password_hash, role)
   - devices (id, name, api_key_hash, last_seen, status)
   - build_jobs (id, component, status, created_at, completed_at)
   - flash_jobs (id, build_job_id, device_id, status, created_at)
   - build_logs (id, build_job_id, timestamp, line, level)
   - flash_history (id, flash_job_id, result, duration, error_message)

